Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:08:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 47/61] docs: NNS.dep asym orientation and p.value; NNS.part
 labels and points

NNS.dep (roxygen + Rd):
- asym: describe what TRUE does (partition on x, dependence of y on x)
  instead of 'FALSE (default) Allows for asymmetrical dependencies'.
- note: the asymmetric matrix entry [i, j] is row i ---> column j
  (verified: NNS.dep(cbind(x, x^2), asym = TRUE)$Dependence[1, 2] =
  NNS.dep(x, x^2, asym = TRUE) = 0.765, the reverse is 0.405); the note
  said column ---> row.
- p.value: describe the permutation p-values (upper tail for Dependence)
  and that plotting needs print.map = TRUE.
NNS.part (roxygen + Rd): document the quadrant digit coding relative to
the gravity centres (XY: 1 upper-right, 2 upper-left, 3 lower-right,
4 lower-left; XONLY: 1 low, 2 high; verified by tabulating against
NNS.gravity), that regression points are one per prior.quadrant, and
that the returned order can be below the requested one.
Rd files regenerated with roxygen2 from the edited sources.
Documentation only.
---
 R/Dependence.R    |  6 +++---
 R/Partition_Map.R | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 man/NNS.dep.Rd    |  6 +++---
 man/NNS.part.Rd   | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/R/Dependence.R b/R/Dependence.R
index cbf6298..07da910 100644
--- a/R/Dependence.R
+++ b/R/Dependence.R
@@ -4,13 +4,13 @@
 #'
 #' @param x a numeric vector, matrix or data frame.
 #' @param y \code{NULL} (default) or a numeric vector with compatible dimensions to \code{x}.
-#' @param asym logical; \code{FALSE} (default) Allows for asymmetrical dependencies.
-#' @param p.value logical; \code{FALSE} (default) Generates 100 independent random permutations to test results against and plots 95 percent confidence intervals along with all results.
+#' @param asym logical; \code{FALSE} (default) returns the symmetric measures. If \code{TRUE}, returns the asymmetric (directional) measures: the partition is built on \code{x} only and the result measures the dependence of \code{y} on \code{x} (\code{y} as a function of \code{x}); swap the arguments for the other direction.
+#' @param p.value logical; \code{FALSE} (default) If \code{TRUE} (bivariate only), compares the results against 100 random permutations of \code{y}: the Dependence p-value is the upper-tail permutation p-value \code{(1 + #(null >= observed)) / (1 + 100)}, the Correlation p-value is the smaller of the two one-sided tail frequencies, and the 95 percent intervals of the permutation null are returned (and plotted when \code{print.map = TRUE}).
 #' @param print.map logical; \code{FALSE} (default) Plots quadrant means, or p-value replicates.
 #' @return Returns the bi-variate \code{"Correlation"} and \code{"Dependence"} or correlation / dependence matrix for matrix input.
 #'
 #' @note
-#' For asymmetrical \code{(asym = TRUE)} matrices, directional dependence is returned as ([column variable] ---> [row variable]).
+#' For asymmetrical \code{(asym = TRUE)} matrices, entry \code{[i, j]} is the directional dependence ([row variable i] ---> [column variable j]), i.e. \code{NNS.dep(x[, i], x[, j], asym = TRUE)}, the dependence of column \code{j} on row variable \code{i}.
 #'
 #' @author Fred Viole, OVVO Financial Systems
 #' @references Viole, F. and Nawrocki, D. (2013) "Nonlinear Nonparametric Statistics: Using Partial Moments" (ISBN: 1490523995, 2nd edition: \url{https://ovvo-financial.github.io/NNS/book/})
diff --git a/R/Partition_Map.R b/R/Partition_Map.R
index c7d6318..ca5f86b 100644
--- a/R/Partition_Map.R
+++ b/R/Partition_Map.R
@@ -14,6 +14,25 @@
 #' @param noise.reduction One of "mean", "median", "mode", "mode_class", or "off".
 #'
 #' @return A list containing `order`, `dt`, and `regression.points`.
+#' \itemize{
+#'   \item{\code{order}} the order actually completed. It can be smaller than
+#'   the requested \code{order} when \code{obs.req} / \code{min.obs.stop}
+#'   stop the recursion (e.g. \code{order = 3} returns 2 for \code{n = 200}
+#'   with the default \code{obs.req = 8}).
+#'   \item{\code{dt}} the observations with their final \code{quadrant} and
+#'   \code{prior.quadrant} labels.
+#'   \item{\code{regression.points}} one (x, y) centroid per
+#'   \code{prior.quadrant}, i.e. per cell of the previous order: \code{order = 1}
+#'   gives 4 final quadrants but a single regression point (\code{"q"}),
+#'   \code{order = 2} gives up to 16 quadrants and 4 points.
+#' }
+#' @details
+#' Quadrant labels append one digit per order. Cells are split at the
+#' \link{NNS.gravity} centre of each coordinate (not the mean). For the
+#' default joint partition (\code{type = NULL}) the digit is
+#' \code{1 + (x <= cx) + 2 * (y <= cy)}: 1 = upper-right, 2 = upper-left,
+#' 3 = lower-right, 4 = lower-left. For \code{type = "XONLY"} the digit is
+#' 1 for \code{x <= cx} and 2 for \code{x > cx}.
 #' @export
 #' 
 #' 
